  "body": "Add one page listing every keyboard shortcut and mouse action in CamCraft, with a column each for Windows/Linux and macOS.\n\nCover:\n- File, Edit and Run shortcuts (new, open model, open project, save, save as, post, undo, redo, copy and paste an operation, delete, frame/fit);\n- the viewport mouse (orbit, pan, zoom, and the trackpad equivalents on a Mac);\n- picking modifiers (add an edge, pick a whole loop, box-select, deselect);\n- right-click and context menus (Control-click or two-finger click on a Mac).\n\nTake the bindings from the code (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/panes.rs`, `edge_pick.rs`, `interact.rs`, the ribbon tips), not from memory. Where the app uses egui's `command` modifier, the macOS column is Cmd. Where it reads the real Ctrl, check on a Mac whether Control-click arrives as a right-click, and say so.\n\nRelated: #1236 (Mac equivalents throughout the site) finds the Windows-only wording on other pages; this page is the one table those pages can link to.\n\nDone means: a shortcuts and mouse page in the guide, every entry checked against the code, with Mac and Windows/Linux columns, linked from first-run.md.\n",
